const enBody = `
<header>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-2">Last verified: 2026-09-02 against <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/claude-fable-and-mythos-5-1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Anthropic's launch post</a> and <a href="https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">docs.anthropic.com pricing</a>.</p>
  <p class="text-lg text-gray-700">Anthropic dropped Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1 on September 1, 2026 — the same model weights with two different safeguard profiles. The actual pricing change is small ($10/$50 per million input/output tokens stays put), but the cache-read tier was cut 75%, the new Enterprise Frontier Safeguards (EFS) tier delivers customer-controlled zero-data-retention, and on agentic benchmarks Fable 5.1 leapfrogs Fable 5 enough that Anthropic itself recommends Fable 5.1 over Opus 5 for "demanding reasoning and long-horizon agentic work." This article walks through the verified launch facts, the pricing tier shifts, the API migration recipe, and the developer-experience changes that matter.</p>
</header>

<section>
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">What Just Launched (September 1, 2026)</h2>
  <p>The September 1 launch is a single model family with two SKUs:</p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 text-gray-700">
    <li><strong>Claude Fable 5.1</strong> — generally available via the API under <code>claude-fable-5-1</code>. Carries Anthropic's standard production safeguards. Available in claude.ai, Claude Code, Claude Cowork, and the public API.</li>
    <li><strong>Claude Mythos 5.1</strong> — same weights, tighter cyber and biology safeguards. Available only through trusted-access programs for vetted cyber defenders and life scientists. Initially limited to US organizations; Anthropic is coordinating with the US government to expand to international partners.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The launch announcement (HN front page on 2026-09-01 with 913 points / 859 comments) is anchored on three concrete moves versus Fable 5:</p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 text-gray-700">
    <li><strong>Cache read pricing cut 75%.</strong> Where Fable 5 charged $1.00/MTok for cache reads (the most common cost component in long agent runs), Fable 5.1 charges $0.25/MTok. For a typical workload this drops Fable 5.1's effective cost about 25% below Fable 5; for highly agentic tasks the savings reach 45%.</li>
    <li><strong>Enterprise Frontier Safeguards (EFS).</strong> A new architecture that stores request and response data in customer-controlled cloud infrastructure rather than Anthropic's servers. It delivers zero-data-retention-equivalent privacy while still letting Anthropic's classifiers run on the streamed prompts.</li>
    <li><strong>Smarter safeguards.</strong> Cybersecurity false positives dropped 60% on the new classifier. In biology, Fable 5.1 is approved for vulnerability discovery (but not exploit development). Mythos 5.1 is the variant that adds biology research access through a US-government-coordinated program.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Pricing: What Actually Changed</h2>
  <p>The base rates are unchanged from Fable 5. The new economics live in the cache tier and the new EFS add-on pricing for the enterprise data-residency tier:</p>
  <table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-gray-200 my-4 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
    <thead class="bg-gray-50">
      <tr>
        <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Tier</th>
        <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Fable 5</th>
        <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Fable 5.1 / Mythos 5.1</th>
        <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Change</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200 text-sm text-gray-700">
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Base input</td><td class="px-4 py-2">$10 / MTok</td><td class="px-4 py-2">$10 / MTok</td><td class="px-4 py-2">unchanged</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Output</td><td class="px-4 py-2">$50 / MTok</td><td class="px-4 py-2">$50 / MTok</td><td class="px-4 py-2">unchanged</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">5-minute cache write</td><td class="px-4 py-2">$12.50 / MTok</td><td class="px-4 py-2">$12.50 / MTok</td><td class="px-4 py-2">unchanged</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">1-hour cache write</td><td class="px-4 py-2">$20 / MTok</td><td class="px-4 py-2">$20 / MTok</td><td class="px-4 py-2">unchanged</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Cache read / hit</td><td class="px-4 py-2">$1.00 / MTok</td><td class="px-4 py-2 font-bold text-blue-700">$0.25 / MTok</td><td class="px-4 py-2 font-bold text-blue-700">-75%</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The 75% cache-read cut is the entire pricing story for most workloads. Anthropic's own decomposition shows that in a typical Claude Code session cache reads dominate the bill; in a long-running research agent that re-uses accumulated context, cache reads can exceed 70% of total spend. Cutting that tier from $1 to $0.25 is what produces the 25% typical / 45% agentic savings. The base input and output rates are not touched.</p>
  <p>Compared to the rest of the Claude lineup as of September 2, 2026:</p>
  <table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-gray-200 my-4 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
    <thead class="bg-gray-50">
      <tr>
        <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Model</th>
        <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Input $/MTok</th>
        <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Output $/MTok</th>
