    <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200 text-sm text-gray-700">
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1</td><td class="px-4 py-2 font-bold text-blue-700">~52%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">~24%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">~30%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">Agentic scientific research</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Terminal-Bench 4.0</td><td class="px-4 py-2 font-bold text-blue-700">~64%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">~52%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">~55%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">Agentic terminal coding</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">OSWorld 2.0 (partial)</td><td class="px-4 py-2 font-bold text-blue-700">77.9%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">72.9%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">75.4%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">Computer use</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">OSWorld 2.0 (strict)</td><td class="px-4 py-2 font-bold text-blue-700">41.7%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">36.1%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">39.6%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">Computer use</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">CursorBench 3.2.0</td><td class="px-4 py-2 font-bold text-blue-700">75%+</td><td class="px-4 py-2">~67%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">~72%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">Agentic IDE</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">GDPval-AA v2 (knowledge work)</td><td class="px-4 py-2 font-bold text-blue-700">1853</td><td class="px-4 py-2">1723</td><td class="px-4 py-2">1824</td><td class="px-4 py-2">Knowledge work parity</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Humanity's Last Exam (no tools)</td><td class="px-4 py-2">60.9%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">57.8%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">56.6%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">Multidisciplinary reasoning</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Humanity's Last Exam (with tools)</td><td class="px-4 py-2">65.0%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">63.8%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">63.6%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">Multidisciplinary reasoning</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">AutomationBench</td><td class="px-4 py-2 font-bold text-blue-700">31.4%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">17.1%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">26.9%</td><td class="px-4 py-2">Business workflows</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>The two biggest jumps are on Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1 (a new agentic-science benchmark where Fable 5.1 more than doubles Fable 5's score at max effort) and on AutomationBench (a workflow-automation benchmark where Fable 5.1 nearly doubles Fable 5). The smallest gap is on Humanity's Last Exam, where Fable 5.1 edges Fable 5 by ~3 percentage points with tools. Across the suite, Fable 5.1 at max effort is roughly equal to Opus 5 at max effort on reasoning-heavy tasks, and substantially better on agentic-coding and agentic-science workloads — Anthropic explicitly recommends Fable 5.1 over Opus 5 for that profile.</p>
  <p>On the effort axis specifically: Fable 5.1 supports five effort levels (low / medium / high / xhigh / max). Fable 5.1 <em>defaults</em> to high effort inside Claude Code and to medium effort in Claude Cowork and on claude.ai. Lower-effort runs are cheaper but less accurate; for coding agents the cost-vs-quality curve favors high or xhigh. The Anthropic prompt-engineering guide for Fable 5.1 walks through the cost-quality trade-off per workload.</p>
